window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AFTER_REBIRTH_I_WAS_FORCED_TO_BECOME_THE_MAFIA_PRINCESS_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":901,"title":"Chapter 901: 902. One Brooch, I Concede.","paragraphs":["The first day of the Lunar New Year.","Weibo’s hot searches exploded.","#A Million-Yuan Lucky Bag Has Been Won# — Trending!","#Elderly Man from the Mountains Wins One Million# — Trending!","#Has ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍WeTalk Crashed?# — Boiling!","#I Shook for Three Minutes and Only Got Sixty-Eight Cents# — Boiling!","#Longfutong Linked More Than Fifty-Three Million Bank Cards# — Hot!","An official Weibo announcement confirmed that, in a remote mountain village in BS Province, an elderly man had won a million-yuan lucky bag. For privacy reasons, however, his identity had not been disclosed.","The moment the news came out, the comments section erupted.","“Holy crap! One million! An actual million yuan in cash!”","“That old man from the mountains became a millionaire with one casual shake, while I shook for ten minutes and only got five yuan and twenty cents. Is this what they call fate?”","“Be grateful for your five yuan. I only got three. I feel like WeTalk is psychologically manipulating me.”","“You’re all focused on the wrong thing. The real point is Longfutong. How long has it been? Its number of linked bank cards has already shot past fifty-three million. Do you know what that means? It took Taobao seven or eight years to build up its payment users, and Longfutong nearly caught up overnight.”","“Taobao: Is there no justice left in this world? I’ve spent seven or eight years building a payment platform, and they caught up in one night.”","“Looks like Ma Yunyun won’t be getting any sleep tonight.”","“Ma Yunyun: Why am I the one getting splashed when you two are fighting?”","“Seriously, don’t you find this terrifying? WeTalk launched a red-packet campaign and actually tied the two Mas together before pinning them to the ground. That’s absolutely brutal!”","“......”","Hangzhou. Taobao headquarters.","The New Year duty roster was normally divided into shifts. In previous years, only about half the employees would have been working at this time.","But this year, not a single person in the payments department had taken leave. Everyone was in the office.","Even Ma Yunyun himself had come in and was personally watching the real-time data on the giant screen.","Two curves were engaged in a fierce chase.","The blue line represented the number of users who had linked bank cards to their payment platform. After seven or eight years, that number had accumulated to more than eighty million.","The red line represented the number of users who had linked bank cards to Longfutong.","Before New Year’s Eve, the red curve had stood at only one-tenth of the blue one.","But from the period before New Year’s Eve onward, the red line began climbing at an almost vertical angle, as if it had been injected with stimulants.","Ten million. Twenty million. Thirty million...","It kept surging until it passed fifty million.","Today, the red line officially broke through the sixty-million mark, leaving it only a little more than twenty million behind the blue line.","“We’ve been doing this for seven or eight years.”","“They caught up in a single Spring Festival.”","Ma Yunyun watched as the members of the payments team sat in silence, their expressions complicated. But he did not blame them.","“I don’t blame any of you.”","“Wanlong Group’s Spring Festival Gala red-packet campaign was indeed an ingenious move. It caught us completely off guard, and it’s absolutely worth studying and reflecting on.”","“President Ma, could we launch a similar campaign?” the head of the marketing department asked.","Ma Yunyun shook his head. “We could, but it would have to wait until next Spring Festival. Doing it now wouldn’t mean anything. They already control the pace.”","He paused, then suddenly let out a laugh. “I, Ma Yunyun, have worked in the internet industry for so many years, and this is the first time someone has beaten me so thoroughly that I couldn’t even fight back. That Liu Yutong really is a genius. I concede.”","Everyone present exchanged glances.","Who was Ma Yunyun?","He was the madman universally acknowledged by the internet industry. When he was running Alibaba, he had dared to go head-to-head with eBay. When he entered the payments industry, he had dared to challenge the banks.","The entire business world of Longguo probably couldn’t produce a second person who could make him say, “I concede.”","“Technical team, listen up.”","“Here!”","“Starting tomorrow, put all your effort into developing a red-packet function. The features must be comprehensive, the experience must be smooth, and the interface must be stable. We must be able to do everything WeTalk can do—and whatever WeTalk can’t do, we must find a way to do as well.”","“Yes!”","Ma Yunyun took one last look at the red line still shooting upward on the giant screen, then turned and left the war room.","In the corridor, he pulled out his phone and opened WeTalk. He stared at the blue-green globe icon for a long time.","Then he held down the icon and tapped Uninstall.","After uninstalling it, he stood there silently for ten seconds before downloading WeTalk again from the app store.","Forget it. He’d give Liu Yutong some face.","............","Shencheng. GooseChat headquarters.","The ashtray on Pony Ma’s desk was already stuffed with cigarette butts, and the air was thick with tobacco smoke.","Pony Ma normally didn’t smoke much, but today he had already gone through more than half a pack.","On the computer screen before him were the figures sent over by his subordinates.","On New Year’s Eve, GooseChat had barely managed to gain five million new users.","Under normal circumstances, that would have been an excellent result. But compared with WeTalk’s more than forty million new users, those five million looked completely insignificant.","And if they counted from when WeTalk began its Five Blessings collection campaign before New Year’s Eve, its growth was far more than forty million.","Looking at the number of new users, Pony Ma suddenly felt like laughing.","A little over a month ago, Liu Yutong had told him, “Within two months, WeTalk’s user base will exceed GooseChat’s by at least thirty million.”","At the time, he had thought that goal was impossible.","Now, only a month and a half had passed, and the gap had probably already exceeded the target by nearly twice that amount.","“President Ma.”","The secretary entered carrying a cup of hot tea. “You haven’t slept all night. Why don’t you get some rest?”","“No need. How far has the data been updated?”","“WeTalk has just released its latest figures. Its total number of registered users has surpassed 120 million.”","Pony Ma nodded. “Got it. You can leave.”","After the secretary left, he was once again alone in the office.","Pony Ma took out the dark-gold invitation to the Dark Phoenix Society and examined it for a long time. At last, he opened it and removed the letter and the token inside.","The letter itself was nothing special. It merely contained the invitation.","The important item was the token—a brooch.","The brooch was only about the size of a thumb, and its design was identical to the black phoenix on the letter: wings spread, head lowered, red eyes glaring.","He had no idea what material it was made of, but it felt surprisingly heavy in his hand.","Pony Ma stared at the brooch for a long time.","Finally, he picked up his phone and sent Liu Yutong a text message.","It contained only five words.","I lost. I’ll fly over tomorrow.","............","The morning of the first day of the New Year.","When Liu Yutong received Pony Ma’s text, she was back in her hometown setting off fireworks with Yaya.","Yaya was wearing a red padded jacket and clutching a handful of sparklers. She hopped and bounced around in the open space. Even though fireworks were nowhere near as beautiful in the daytime as they were at night, she was still having the time of her life.","“Big Sister, what do you think the Nian beast looks like?” Yaya asked, turning around while waving her sparkler.","“Probably like a really, really big dog.”","“Then why is it afraid of firecrackers?”","“Because firecrackers are too loud. Its ears can’t stand them.”","“Oh...” Yaya suddenly understood. “So the Nian beast isn’t actually bad. Its ears are just bigger, so it’s more afraid of loud noises?”","Liu Yutong laughed.","“That’s right. The Nian beast isn’t bad. Its ears are just bigger, and it’s more sensitive to loud sounds.”","“Then I won’t call it the Nian beast anymore. I’ll call it Big Dog Whose Ears Hate Loud Noises.”","Yaya was very pleased with the new name she had chosen for herself. She raised the spent sparkler and began running around the courtyard again.","Watching her little figure dart back and forth, Liu Yutong couldn’t help reminding her, “Be careful. Don’t fall.”","Just then, the phone in her pocket vibrated.","She pulled it out and saw a text message on the screen.","It contained only a few simple words.","[I lost. I’ll fly over tomorrow.]","After reading the message, Liu Yutong calmly slipped the phone back into her pocket, then waved to Yaya.","“Yaya, come here. I’ll show you how to set off a big one.”","“What big one?”","Liu Yutong found a cylindrical firework inside the house and placed it on the stone slab in the middle of the courtyard. Then she crouched down and lit the fuse with a lighter.","The fuse hissed and burned as the sisters backed away several steps together.","Three seconds later, a silver burst of light shot from the firework and exploded into a huge golden flower.","Then came a second burst, followed by a third... Silver and red fireworks continued exploding in succession above the courtyard, creating a breathtaking display.","“Wow!”","“Big Sister, these fireworks are so beautiful! What are they called?”","“These are called ‘A Courtyard Full of Red.’”"]},{"number":902,"title":"Chapter 902: 903, Sign the Letter of Intent","paragraphs":["The second day of the Lunar New Year, in Mingzhu City.","When Pony Ma’s private car pulled up in front of Shunchang Tower, he glanced out the window and froze.","The entrance to Shunchang Tower was packed with people.","They were all dressed in identical black suits, each wearing the same silver dragon-shaped badge. From the entrance all the way to the roadside, they stood in two perfectly orderly rows—at least two or three hundred of them.","With that kind of spectacle and oppressive presence, anyone who didn’t know better might have thought a foreign head of state had come for a visit.","The corner of Pony Ma’s mouth twitched.","He couldn’t tell whether Liu Yutong had arranged such an elaborate welcome for him or was trying to give him a show of force.","Probably both.","“P-President Ma, we’re here,” the driver said cautiously.","Pony Ma took a deep breath and pushed open the door.","The moment he stepped out, the two rows of men in black turned their heads in perfect unison. Hundreds of eyes landed on him at once.","For one brief moment, Pony Ma seriously considered sitting right back down in the car.","Just then, there was movement by the entrance to Shunchang Tower.","Liu Yutong came out to greet him.","She was wearing another black suit today, with that distinctive solid-gold dragon-shaped badge pinned to her chest. Her long hair fell loosely over her shoulders, and a faint smile rested on her face.","Yun Cheng and Lan Die followed half a step behind her. Behind them was a group of core members wearing platinum-colored badges, every one of them carrying an extraordinary air.","“President Ma, Happy New Year,” Liu Yutong said as she approached and extended her hand.","Pony ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍Ma hurried forward and took it. “Director Liu, Happy New Year. This reception of yours... I’m honestly overwhelmed by the honor.”","“President Ma is an esteemed guest. It’s only proper.” Liu Yutong smiled faintly and gestured toward the building. “Please, come inside.”","The two of them walked into Shunchang Tower side by side, followed by the rows of men in black.","As he walked, Pony Ma couldn’t help reflecting to himself.","He had been dealing with Liu Yutong for quite some time, but every meeting with her managed to shock him all over again.","The elevator rose all the way to the forty-eighth floor.","When the conference-room door opened, several people were already inside.","Zhang Dalong, head of WeChat and one of the central figures in the merger negotiations.","Zhao Tianyi, chief legal officer of the Wanlong Association Group, wearing his trademark gold-rimmed glasses.","The other two were the heads of legal and finance who had flown in ahead of time from Big Goose. They were both Pony Ma’s trusted aides, and at that moment they sat stiffly upright.","They hadn’t expected the Wanlong Association headquarters to be this intimidating. Everywhere they looked, there were men in black.","“President Ma, please take a seat.” Liu Yutong sat down at the head of the table.","Pony Ma took the seat opposite her. One glance at the documents on the table was enough for him to understand roughly what was coming.","“President Ma, what do you have to say about the bet we made before?” Liu Yutong asked.","Pony Ma gave a bitter laugh. “Director Liu, there’s nothing left to say. I concede. And I concede wholeheartedly.”","Even now, thinking about that bet made his face burn with embarrassment.","Two months earlier, Liu Yutong had told him that WeChat would surpass GooseChat by thirty million users within two months.","At the time, he had thought the woman must be out of her mind. GooseChat had the enormous traffic pool of QQ behind it. The difference between the two platforms was only a few million users. How could WeChat possibly open up a thirty-million-user lead in just two months?","And then what happened?","Liu Yutong threw ten billion yuan into a Spring Festival red-envelope campaign, and the entire country went crazy.","On New Year’s Eve, Pony Ma had watched with his own eyes as WeChat’s new-user curve shot upward at an almost vertical angle. There was no stopping it.","When he checked the results on the morning of the first day of the new year, WeChat’s registered users had soared to 120 million, while GooseChat was still hovering around sixty million.","What was even more outrageous was that the red-envelope campaign had also managed to knock Old Ma flat in the process.","LongPay’s number of users with linked bank cards had surged by tens of millions over the course of the holiday. The defensive moat that Taobao had spent seven or eight years building had nearly been blasted flat by a single Spring Festival campaign.","Honestly, Pony Ma even felt a little sorry for Old Ma.","The man had only wanted to watch the show from the sidelines. He hadn’t provoked anyone or done anything wrong.","“President Ma, you’re being too serious. Business competition is like that. Sometimes you win, sometimes you lose. It’s perfectly normal.” Liu Yutong turned and nodded at Zhao Tianyi. “Tianyi, let’s begin.”","Zhao Tianyi adjusted his gold-rimmed glasses, opened the thick stack of documents in front of him, cleared his throat, and began reading through the key clauses of the merger agreement one by one.","“Clause One: WeChat will retain independent brand operations, while GooseChat will be incorporated into WeChat.”","Pony Ma nodded slightly.","They had already reached a consensus on this point. Once WeChat was folded into Big Goose, there would be no reason to keep GooseChat. Otherwise, it would simply be a waste of resources.","“Clause Two: Mr. Zhang Dalong will continue to serve concurrently as president of the WeChat division and report to the board of directors of Big Goose Group. The WeChat team will retain an independent organizational structure, with its offices located in Mingzhu City.”","At this, Pony Ma couldn’t help giving Zhang Dalong a long, deep look.","He regretted more than ever letting this man leave back then. If Zhang Dalong were still at Goose Factory, how could any of this have happened? WeChat might have been his product by now.","Of course, he had no idea that Zhang Dalong had also been in an extremely difficult position at the time.","“Clause Three: The Wanlong Association Group will contribute all of WeChat’s assets, along with an additional cash investment, in exchange for a thirty-percent stake in Big Goose Group, thereby becoming its largest shareholder.”","Pony Ma’s eyelid twitched violently.","Thirty percent.","He understood better than anyone what that figure meant.","Big Goose’s ownership structure was already highly dispersed. Nanfei, the foreign corporation, held more than thirty percent. He and several members of the founding team held only a little over ten percent combined, while the rest consisted of scattered shares traded on the secondary market.","Now Liu Yutong was suddenly going to become the largest shareholder. That meant Nanfei would have to give way—or even be forced out entirely.","More importantly, who knew whether The Young Lady would go completely mad and continue buying up shares on the secondary market, increasing her stake step by step until she achieved outright control?","If that happened, he really would be finished.","But that was a problem for later. He had lost the bet, and when you lost, you had to accept it.","For now, all he could do was find a way to place restrictions in the agreement and prevent her from increasing her stake without limits.","Of course, it was still too early to discuss that.","“Director Liu, how do you intend to deal with Nanfei?”","That was exactly the question Liu Yutong had been waiting for.","“Since you’re here, President Ma, I’ll be direct. I’d like to ask you to personally invite the people from Nanfei to come to Mingzhu City.”","“Tell them you’re inviting them to watch the Longteng Cup final on the day of the Lantern Festival.”","Pony Ma: “...”","Invite them to watch a match?","Looking at the smile on her face, Pony Ma suddenly felt a chill run down his back. Surely this woman wasn’t planning to seize control by force?","“Director Liu, you’re not thinking of...”","“Don’t worry, President Ma. We’re a legitimate private enterprise. We never do anything illegal.”","“I merely want to give our foreign friend an up-close experience of the Wanlong Association’s corporate culture. That’s all.”","Corporate culture.","When those four words came from Liu Yutong’s mouth, Pony Ma found them unnerving no matter how he interpreted them.","He couldn’t help recalling the rumors about the Ten Thousand Dragons Society—stories about fleets of hundreds of identical luxury sedans, thousands of men in black surrounding powerful underworld figures, and people being forced to jump from buildings in front of the police...","Forget it. No point thinking about it.","The more he thought about it, the harder it would be to fall asleep.","Pony Ma finally agreed. “All right. I’ll contact him as soon as I get back and ask him to come over.”","It wasn’t as if he was the one playing the villain. He was only passing along a message.","Liu Yutong nodded. “Tianyi, continue.”","Zhao Tianyi pushed up his glasses and went on reading the remaining clauses.","“Clause Four: Mr. Ma will continue to serve as chairman and CEO of Big Goose Group, and his authority over the company’s day-to-day operations and management will not be interfered with.”","Pony Ma felt slightly relieved when he heard this.","At least on the surface, he would still be the captain of Big Goose. He would still have his hands on the wheel.","But before he could fully relax, Zhao Tianyi immediately read the next clause.","“Clause Five: Ms. Liu Yutong undertakes never to increase her shareholding. However, as the largest shareholder, she will have veto power over major strategic decisions.”","Pony Ma’s expression instantly became a sight to behold.","“You call that not interfering with day-to-day operations? You even want veto power!”","“I’m only making sure no one takes advantage of you. That’s called supervision,” Liu Yutong said matter-of-factly.","“What are you supervising?”","“Making sure you don’t make foolish decisions.”","Liu Yutong casually gave him a few examples. “For instance, how Big Goose nearly sold QQ for one million back then. Or how your company actually dared to pay employees in cryptocurrency. And the whole forced either-or fiasco... Haven’t you people made enough foolish decisions already?”","Pony Ma: “...”","He wanted to argue, but every one of those things had really happened.","Zhao Tianyi continued reading the clauses that followed.","There were anti-dilution protections, preemptive subscription rights, arrangements for board seats, and more. Each provision was laid out in meticulous detail, leaving no loopholes unaddressed.","The more Pony Ma listened, the more alarmed he became.","This agreement had taken every possible loophole into consideration. There was no way their legal team could have drafted something so comprehensive without preparing for several months.","In other words, Liu Yutong hadn’t set her sights on Big Goose on a whim. She had been plotting this for a long time.","After all the clauses had been read, Zhao Tianyi closed the document and said calmly, “If neither of you has any objections, you may sign.”","Pony Ma picked up the pen and paused for several seconds over the signature line.","Once he signed, Big Goose would change forever.","The empire he had founded and painstakingly managed for more than a decade would now have another, even more formidable major shareholder.","But in the end, he gritted his teeth and signed his name with a series of quick strokes.","Liu Yutong took the pen and signed her name as well.","The two exchanged the documents and signed them again.","Zhang Dalong, Zhao Tianyi, and the legal and financial representatives from Big Goose then signed in turn.","Of course, what they were signing for the moment was only a letter of intent. Nan Fei’s shares had yet to be acquired, and given the significance of the matter, everything had to remain confidential at this stage.","Only after the situation with Nan Fei had been completely settled would the agreement officially take effect.","Still, this marked a crucial first step.","From this day forward, it could be said that Liu Yutong had effectively taken control of most of Long Kingdom’s internet industry.","Liu Yutong stood and extended her hand toward Pony Ma. “President Ma, we’re family from now on.”","Pony Ma shook her hand, his smile somewhat strained. “Director Liu, I’ll be counting on your guidance from now on.”","“Of course.”","Liu Yutong released his hand, then suddenly thought of something.","“Oh, right, President Ma. When Nan Fei’s largest shareholder arrives, please come along and help receive him. After all, you’ve worked together for so many years. It would be more appropriate for you to be there.”","Pony Ma: “...”","Receive him? What kind of reception was this?","Why didn’t she receive the person she had invited herself? Why did she have to drag him into it?","A sudden, ominous feeling came over him.","Something major was bound to happen on the day of the Lantern Festival."]},{"number":903,"title":"Chapter 903: 904. Van der Burgh Arrives","paragraphs":["On the seventh day of the Lunar New Year, with the festive atmosphere still lingering, the internet industry had already exploded.","Big Goose Group’s stock price entered free fall. From HK$280 billion before New Year’s Eve, it plunged through HK$200 billion within just a few trading days, then dropped again to HK$160 billion. Its market capitalization had nearly been cut in half, dragging the entire Hong Kong technology sector down with it and leaving investors everywhere in despair.","Panic spread throughout the market.","The reason was actually quite simple.","After ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‍WeTalk’s massive red-envelope campaign on New Year’s Eve, everyone had realized one thing: Big Goose was probably never going to catch up with WeTalk in the mobile-social arena.","This wasn’t a matter of being slightly behind. It was an entirely different dimension.","WeTalk’s registered users had soared to 130 million, with daily active users holding steadily above 40 million. GooseChat, meanwhile, was still struggling around the 60-million mark.","Even more disastrous was the fact that GooseChat users spent only one-fifth as much time on the app each day as WeTalk users.","One-fifth.","What did that mean?","It meant that even when users reluctantly installed GooseChat on their phones, they rarely opened it. And when they did, they would take a quick glance before closing it again. There was simply no chance of building any real social engagement.","The capital markets had always voted with their feet. The moment investors sensed that the wind was changing, they began selling off their holdings regardless of the cost. Big Goose’s stock plunged like a kite with a severed string, without even the slightest meaningful rebound.","“Big Goose Is Finished!”","Those four words had practically become the headline of every financial newspaper.","“The Mobile-Social Landscape Is Settled: The Twilight of the Big Goose Empire Has Arrived.”","“WeTalk Ascendant, GooseChat Forced Out.”","“Pony Ma’s Waterloo: From Four Hundred Billion to One Hundred Sixty Billion in Just Six Months.”","One bearish headline after another flooded the media.","At Big Goose’s headquarters in Shencheng, the executives looked utterly dispirited. Every meeting was shrouded in a dead, gloomy silence.","Pony Ma, however, remained surprisingly calm. He showed up at the office on time every day, held his meetings, signed his documents, and carried on as though the storm of negative coverage had nothing to do with him.","Only his secretary and a handful of trusted aides knew that Pony Ma had already reached a private agreement with Liu Yutong of the Wanlong Association.","During the days when Big Goose’s stock had fallen to its lowest point, a rumor suddenly began circulating through investment circles.","The Wanlong Association Group intended to acquire all the shares held by Big Goose’s largest shareholder, Nanfly Capital, and take control of Big Goose as its new largest shareholder.","Once the news broke, the financial world erupted again.","“Wanlong Association is going to acquire Big Goose? Am I reading this right? What kind of legendary company is Wanlong Association? First, they crushed Fruit, and now they’re going to swallow Big Goose whole?”","“You’re leaving someone out. They also took Ma Yun’s payment business down a peg.”","“Fruit: What did I ever do to you? Big Goose: I didn’t do anything to you either! Some Treasure: I was just passing by to watch the show. How did I end up covered in blood too?”","“Hilarious. Is Wanlong Association planning to beat up the entire Dragon Nation internet and technology industries? Who’s next? Baidu? NetEase?”","“I’m more curious about where Wanlong Association gets all its money. Ten billion yuan in red envelopes, and acquiring Big Goose’s shares would cost at least tens of billions. Do they print money? They’re ridiculously rich.”","“Don’t forget what Wanlong Association actually does. They’re a perfectly respectable private enterprise. (Dog-head emoji for self-preservation.)”","“As someone from Jinchuan, I can confirm that this company is extremely... respectable.”","“Those black-clad fighters from Wanlong Association are terrifying. I heard they sent thousands of people into Jinchuan and wiped out the local crime boss.”","“Thousands of people... Is this a private enterprise or a criminal organization?”","“Either way, don’t provoke Wanlong Association. Seriously. They’re terrifying.”","“...”","While the domestic internet was still buzzing with heated discussion, thousands of miles away in Amsterdam, at the headquarters of Nanfly Capital, its chairman, the Dutch investor Vanderberg, was sitting in his office and studying a document before him.","It was a formal acquisition offer sent by Wanlong Association Group.","Vanderberg was fifty-seven years old. Born into an old Dutch investment family, he had spent more than twenty years making his way through the Eastern Continent’s markets. He had begun investing in Big Goose back when it was still a small company with only a few dozen employees, and had watched it grow into a Chinese internet giant. The shares he had initially purchased for tens of millions of U.S. dollars were now worth hundreds of billions of Hong Kong dollars.","The investment had been named one of the most successful cases in the history of venture capital in the Eastern Continent by the Financial Times.","Now, someone wanted to use a few hundred billion Hong Kong dollars to rip this cash cow out of his hands by the roots.","It was laughable.","“Ridiculous!”","Vanderberg tossed the document onto the desk, then summoned the head of Nanfly Capital’s Eastern Continent operations.","“Reply to Wanlong Association. Nanfly Capital will not sell a single share of Big Goose. We believed in this company twenty years ago, we still believe in it now, and we’ll continue to believe in it in the future. No matter how much Wanlong Association offers, we won’t sell.”","The executive across from him hesitated before speaking cautiously.","“Chairman, Wanlong Association’s offer is actually at a considerable premium to the current market price. Considering Big Goose’s present stock-price trend and market expectations...”","“Market expectations?”","Vanderberg let out a cold laugh.","“The market expects Big Goose to collapse, and you believe it? The market once expected Amazon to fail too. Look at it now.”","The executive had nothing to say.","Vanderberg rose and walked over to the floor-to-ceiling window. With his hands clasped behind his back, he gazed at Amsterdam’s gray winter sky.","“I’ve invested in the Dragon Nation for twenty years. I’ve met all kinds of people. Some tried to pressure me through connections. Some tried to overwhelm me with money. Others tried to frighten me with underhanded tactics. But in the end, not one of them managed to take something from me that I didn’t want to sell.”","“Wanlong Association—a company founded less than four years ago—wants to acquire my stake in Big Goose? Ha.”","“Let them take their first company public before they start talking.”","“Also, have someone prepare the private jet. I’m going to the Dragon Nation.”","The executive from the Eastern Continent operations department froze.","“You’re going to the Dragon Nation?”","“Yes.”","Vanderberg nodded.","“The Young Lady of Wanlong Association had Pony Ma personally send me an invitation to attend some... Longteng Cup final. I’d like to see for myself exactly what kind of person this young woman is—the one who has thrown the entire Dragon Nation internet industry into chaos. Her appetite is certainly enormous.”","At the same time, at Big Goose’s headquarters in Shencheng, Pony Ma hung up after receiving Vanderberg’s transoceanic call. His expression was complicated.","Vanderberg’s attitude had been even more unyielding than he had expected.","“Pony, I know you’re under tremendous pressure right now, but Nanfly isn’t some retail investor who runs at the first sign of a falling stock price. We’ve worked together for so many years. You should know my style. If Wanlong Association wants to acquire our shares, they can dream on!”","Vanderberg had even comforted Pony Ma in return, telling him that he would fly to the Dragon Nation in a few days to deal with the matter personally. Pony Ma had nothing to worry about. Nanfly would always be Big Goose’s staunchest supporter.","Its staunchest supporter.","Pony Ma nearly lost his composure the second he heard those words.","That shield of yours is probably no match for the other guy's spear!","To this day, Vanderberg still has no idea that Pony Ma himself is one of the hidden masterminds pulling the strings behind this acquisition.","\"What a mess I've gotten myself into!\" Pony Ma leaned back in his chair, pinching the space between his brows.","He felt as if he was being roasted over an open fire.","On one side was Vanderberg's long-standing trust in him, and on the other was the signed letter of intent for the merger that Liu Yutong held in her hands.","Worst of all, he was the one who had to personally coax Vanderberg over to Mingzhu City, while the man had not the slightest clue what was waiting for him there.","After hesitating for a long time, Pony Ma finally picked up his phone and sent Liu Yutong a text message.","[Vanderberg is being very stubborn, but he's agreed to come to Mingzhu City for the Dragon Soaring Cup.]","Less than thirty seconds later, a reply popped up.","[Got it. Great work, Mr. Ma. Once he's here, he'll naturally agree to the terms.]","Reading those words, Pony Ma felt a chill run down his spine.","He had the distinct feeling that he was leading an old friend he'd worked with for years straight into a trap. But there was no turning back now. That signed letter of intent was his token of allegiance, and he'd already put his name to it — there was no way he dared to back out now.","\"Vanderberg, Vanderberg... don't hold this against me...\"","Pony Ma lit a cigarette, took a slow drag, and exhaled the smoke. \"Once you get to Mingzhu City, you'll understand. Some people simply can't be dealt with just by being tough.\"","Several days later at Danan City International Airport.","A Gulfstream G550 private jet slowly touched down on the runway.","When the cabin door opened, Vanderberg stepped down the airstair in a dark gray cashmere coat, followed by the East Regional Director, two assistants, a personal interpreter, and no fewer than seven or eight bodyguards.","Vanderberg was a tall man who habitually held his chin high, carrying the poise and arrogance of an old-school Western investor.","He had fully expected to be greeted on arrival by a horde of menacing men in black, just like the rumors about the Wanlong Society his assistant had dug up online described.","He had even rehearsed a few sharp, sarcastic lines in his head, ready to throw them out the second they met to throw his hosts off balance.","Much to his surprise, though, there were only three cars waiting for him: three ordinary black Mercedes-Benz S-Class sedans, driven by three young men in black suits with silver dragon emblems pinned to their chests.","The drivers looked to be in their early twenties, lean and built, but unfailingly polite. When they saw him, they gave a slight bow and spoke in fluent foreign languages. \"Mr. Vanderberg, welcome to Mingzhu City. The Young Lady has sent us to pick you up.\"","That's it?","Vanderberg sneered to himself.","The rumors were obviously wildly exaggerated. All that talk about convoys of hundreds of Mercedes-Benz and crowds of men in black everywhere — it was all nonsense made up by internet users from Longguo who had clearly never seen the scale of real power.","He climbed into the back of the car, leaned against the plush leather seat, and propped one leg over the other, feeling far more relaxed now.","The car pulled smoothly out of the airport and merged into the highway traffic.","Vanderberg glanced out the window at the city scenery speeding past and casually asked in a foreign language, \"What kind of competition is this Dragon Soaring Cup of yours?\"","The young driver glanced at him in the rearview mirror and smiled. \"It's a martial arts competition, Mr. Vanderberg. It's the Wanlong Society Group's very first annual internal martial arts tournament.\"","\"An internal corporate martial arts tournament?\" Vanderberg raised an eyebrow, nearly laughing out loud.","A legitimate corporation running a martial arts tournament for its staff? It sounded like one of those silly corporate culture events Longguo companies loved to put on, all for show, just a gimmick to drum up so-called team cohesion.","He asked casually, \"How many people are competing in it?\"","\"Roughly ten thousand or so, Mr. Vanderberg,\" the driver answered offhandedly.","???","Vanderberg's leg, which he had propped up, froze mid-motion.","Te... ten thousand people at an internal corporate martial arts tournament?","What kind of company could get ten thousand employees to take part in a fighting competition?","He's got to be making that up.","He was just about to press for more details when the car exited the highway and turned onto a wide six-lane avenue.","A short while later, a massive stadium came into view — the kind that could seat tens of thousands of people.","The entire parking lot surrounding the venue was packed with cars. Vanderberg swept his eyes over them quickly, and saw that almost every single one was a black Mercedes-Benz, lined up row after row across the entire lot. Their license plates had every combination of consecutive numbers and letters imaginable, and there had to be at least a few hundred of them.","The corner of his mouth twitched uncontrollably.","The car pulled to a stop at the stadium's VIP entrance.","The second Vanderberg stepped out, he spotted a familiar figure waiting for him right at the door — Pony Ma.","\"Ma, you're here too?\" Vanderberg said, caught off guard.","The expression on Pony Ma's face was so complicated it looked like he'd been constipated for three days, finally relieved himself, then realized the toilet was clogged.","But he quickly composed himself, put on a bright smile, stepped forward, and shook Vanderberg's hand. \"Mr. Vanderberg, welcome to Mingzhu City. Director Liu specifically asked me to come and keep you company, so you wouldn't get bored watching the competition alone.\"","Vanderberg clapped him on the shoulder and laughed. \"Ma, you look like you haven't been sleeping well. Too much stress lately? Don't worry, I came all the way here to wrap up this Wanlong Society acquisition once and for all. I give you my word, Nanfei won't sell a single share of Big Goose's stock.\"","Pony Ma's smile was more pained than a sob. \"Thanks a lot.\"","Vanderberg then followed Pony Ma and the two men in black toward the VIP passage, walked down the red-carpeted corridor, and pushed open the heavy soundproof door.","The moment he stepped inside the stadium, he froze completely in place, feeling as if he had just fallen straight into an ice cellar."]},{"number":904,"title":"Chapter 904: 905. An Unparalleled Formation","paragraphs":["Vanderberg stood at the entrance to the VIP passageway, staring at the scene before him in utter shock.","Before entering Long Nation, he had secretly looked down on the Wanlong Association. After all, it was a company from Long Nation that had been established less than four years ago. How impressive could it really be... Heh...","But the moment he stepped through the stadium entrance, the expression on his face instantly became this:","ヽ(;゚д゚)ノ!!!","The stadium was packed with people.","This was not a figure of speech. It was a literal sea of people.","More than ten thousand men in black occupied the surrounding stands. They all wore identical black suits and identical silver dragon-shaped badges. Starting from the front rows of the lowest tier, they filled the stands level by level, all the way to the very top. Densely packed, they looked from a distance like a vast black ocean.","Even though none of them were doing anything, the sheer presence they gave off simply by sitting there was enough to scare a timid person into having a heart attack.","Vanderberg suddenly felt that his legs were no longer obeying him. They felt as though they had been filled with cement, leaving him unable to move.","Standing beside him, Pony Ma secretly glanced at Vanderberg's stunned, terrified expression. For some reason, he felt incredibly satisfied.","This was fantastic!","When he had first arrived at the stadium and seen so many people in black, his reaction had been almost identical to Vanderberg's.","Now, at last, someone else could experience the same shock he had felt.","\"Mr. Vanderberg, shall we go in?\"","Vanderberg walked stiffly into the stadium and finally got a clear view of the entire venue.","A huge arena had been constructed right in the center of the stadium.","It was nearly half the size of a basketball court, perfectly square, with a platform standing a little over a meter above the ground. Four enormous LED screens surrounded it on all sides.","Suspended directly above the arena was a circular display screen, where three large characters scrolled across it:","—The Dragon Soaring Cup!","Two couplets hung on either side of the arena.","The first read:","Fists and feet reveal the truth; the dragon soars across the four seas.","The second read:","Law and reason determine the universe; the association gathers heroes from every corner.","After hearing the translator explain the meaning of the couplets, Vanderberg felt deeply unsettled.","They gave him the strange impression of being both righteous and sinister.","The sinister part was that these men in black looked far too much like an overseas criminal organization—and on the surface, they seemed countless times more powerful than even the strongest organizations abroad.","The righteous part was that these people apparently studied the law as well?","It was... an extremely contradictory combination.","\"Mr. Vanderberg, your seat is over here.\" The black-clad staff member responsible for guiding him pointed toward several empty seats in the center of the front row.","Vanderberg nodded and slowly made his way over.","With every step he took, he could clearly feel gazes coming at him from all directions.","There was no malice or murderous intent in those eyes, yet they still made the hair on his body rise involuntarily.","His two assistants and eight bodyguards followed behind him. He had brought those bodyguards from Helan. Every one of them stood over 1.9 meters tall and possessed exceptional fighting skills. They would have had no trouble intimidating ordinary thugs.","But compared with the Wanlong Association's black-clad members surrounding them, he suddenly felt that his own bodyguards looked like a flock of quails in suits.","Any one of these people could crush them to pieces with a casual squeeze.","Moreover, the discipline of the Wanlong Association's members was terrifying. Every one of them sat upright, chests out and backs straight, as motionless as statues.","Vanderberg had spent many years in the business world. He had seen plenty of private security teams, including highly disciplined ones, but he had never seen so many people maintain such terrifying discipline at the same time.","Once again, he remembered the information his assistant had gathered about the Wanlong Association before his departure.","[Wanlong Association Group, founded in 2007, with its headquarters in Pearl City. Its founder and chairwoman is Liu Yutong. The group encompasses six major business divisions: commercial retail, technology, digital services, entertainment and media, supply-chain logistics, and financial investment. It has more than two hundred thousand employees...]","The information was formal and official.","But on the final page, his assistant had added several comments copied from internet forums in Long Nation.","[The Wanlong Association? Isn't that the largest organization in Pearl City... No... the largest organization in all of Long Nation?]","[I heard they mobilized four thousand people in BS Province and completely crushed the local crime lord.]","[...]","At the time, Vanderberg had merely laughed after reading those comments. People from Long Nation loved to exaggerate. They loved to boast.","Now, he could not laugh anymore.","Not even a little.","Finally, under the guidance of the staff, he took his seat.","Pony Ma sat to his left, while the seat to his right remained empty. Clearly, it had been reserved for someone even more important.","Vanderberg had barely sat down and had not yet had time to catch his breath when a golden spotlight suddenly descended vertically from the center of the dome, illuminating the middle of the arena.","Whoosh!","More than twelve thousand black-clad members throughout the stadium rose to their feet almost simultaneously.","Vanderberg was startled once again. He had no idea what was happening.","Pony Ma stood up beside him as well. He gently nudged Vanderberg with his elbow and whispered, \"Mr. Vanderberg, you should stand too. It's a rule of the Wanlong Association. Whenever The Young Lady makes an appearance, everyone must rise.\"","The Young Lady.","There was that title again.","Ever since arriving in Long Nation, Vanderberg had heard it countless times.","He was determined to see for himself exactly what kind of person this Young Lady was—the woman everyone kept mentioning.","The moment he stood up, the stadium's domed wraparound screen lit up.","A golden dragon pattern slowly emerged across the enormous LED screen encircling the entire venue. Its body twisted and coiled, its head held high and its eyes wide open, radiating an imposing might as it looked down upon the entire stadium.","As the dragon pattern appeared, a deep drumbeat echoed through the venue.","Boom!","Boom!","Boom!","Every beat was deep and powerful, shaking the blood in their veins until it surged and boiled.","The drumbeats grew faster and more urgent.","Just as they reached their climax, the northern gates of the stadium suddenly opened.","Dozens of black-clad men wearing platinum-colored badges on their chests stepped out first, then lined up on both sides.","Immediately afterward, a man and a woman walked out side by side, guarding the center.","Finally, behind the two guards, a cold, sharp black figure slowly emerged from the shadows, taking one step after another.","She was an extremely young woman dressed in a custom-made black suit. She possessed an overwhelming aura of supreme power, as though she stood above all living things.","A badge was pinned to her chest as well.","A pure-gold dragon-shaped badge.","The badges worn by all twelve thousand people present were either silver or platinum-colored. She alone wore one made of pure gold.","It displayed her unique and unrivaled position.","The instant she appeared, all twelve thousand people lowered their heads in perfect unison. They clenched their left fists and pressed them against their hearts, shouting:","\"Greetings, The Young Lady!\"","“Hello, Young Lady!” shouted more than ten thousand people.","The deafening roar reverberated throughout the venue. Vanderberg instantly felt as if his eardrums were about to burst.","The seven or eight bodyguards he had brought from Helan stood rigidly beside him, their faces pale and their eyes filled with fear and tension.","Pony Ma was little better. Although he had seen members of the Wanlong Association before, this was his first time witnessing such a spectacular scene in person: more than ten thousand men in black saluting a single person at the same time.","The Big Goose Group also had tens of thousands of employees, but the feeling was completely different from what he was seeing now.","When the Big Goose employees saw him, they merely greeted him with ordinary smiles. These people were different. Through their actions, they were telling you directly that as long as The Young Lady gave the order, they would do anything for her.","Yes, anything!","That almost fanatical loyalty was something no normal company possessed. You could search the entire world and still never find anything like it.","“Take your seats.”","Just two casual words.","All twelve thousand people sat down in perfect unison, like a black tide sinking simultaneously.","At the center of the ring, Liu Yutong held a microphone, her voice carried throughout the entire venue by the surround-sound system.","“First of all, congratulations to the two hundred contestants who emerged victorious from among the tens of thousands of core members across the seven major divisions and made it to the stage of the Longteng Cup finals.”","“Every one of you is a source of pride for the Wanlong Association!”","Thunderous applause erupted, spreading through the venue like a tidal wave.","“Next, I would also like to extend my special thanks to the two guests joining us today.”","“Mr. Ma, chairman of the board of the Big Goose Group.”","Pony ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​‍Ma’s name had barely been called before he hurriedly stood up and nodded slightly to the crowd.","“Mr. Vanderberg, chairman of Nanfei Capital.”","The translator relayed the words to Vanderberg, and he immediately stood up, looking just like an elementary school student being called on by his teacher.","As more than ten thousand pairs of eyes focused on him, his heart nearly stopped beating again.","The pressure was insane!!!","At that moment, Vanderberg finally formed an entirely new opinion of the Wanlong Association.","This was not an ordinary company at all.","This damn well was a... XXX!!!","Just as everyone’s attention was fixed on the stage, Liu Yutong announced that the competition was officially beginning.","“The Longteng Cup finals—begin now!”"]}]);
